        "kind": "adjudicated",
        "ref": "adjudication 2026-09-22: rule-level explanation is a capability, not a defect",
        "note": "The predecessor answers 'which rule fired, with which bindings' for ANY derived fact. Verified present: it returns rule_id, rule_text and bindings. The replacement answers only why a FLUENT holds at a time, so this capability was removed rather than relocated. This case exists so the corpus is not selected in the rewrite's favour. The negative control -- the same predicate on a fact that is not derivable -- stops a stub that answers everything from counting as support."
